 ### Global Brick Request Strategy
-The Global Brick Request Strategy is a data-loading heuristic where a ray only requests the bricks absolutely required to satisfy the final rendering request, leaving space in the hash table for other rays [S2]. When a brick is missing, it increments the LoD and looks up the brick at the new resolution, continuing until a missing brick is no longer reported [S2]. Unlike the 'Greedy' strategy, the Global strategy does not request intermediate bricks. It generates the final correct image quickest in terms of raw completion but may produce less pleasing intermediate progress [S2].
